mc(3, 'sewage', `What happens to the BOD as the sewage passes through the aeration tank?`, `It falls, because microbes consume organic matter`, [`It rises, because microbes die`, `It stays the same`, `It becomes zero in primary treatment`], `Microbes in flocs digest the organic matter, so less oxygen will be needed later.`, `Some may think microbes add to BOD, but they remove the organic load.`);
mc(3, 'sewage', `The mixture of gases produced in anaerobic sludge digesters contains`, `methane, hydrogen sulphide and carbon dioxide`, [`only oxygen and nitrogen`, `only chlorine`, `ozone and CFCs`], `This gas mixture is biogas and can be used as an energy source.`);
mc(3, 'biogas', `Which one of the following correctly describes the activity of methanogens in cattle?`, `They break down cellulose in the rumen and give methane`, [`They convert methane into cellulose`, `They fix nitrogen in the intestines`, `They produce penicillin`], `They are anaerobic and part of the gut microbes that digest cellulosic food in ruminants. The same bacteria are used in biogas plants.`);
mc(3, 'biogas', `A biogas plant has`, `a concrete tank with a slurry of dung, a floating cover, a gas outlet and a slurry outlet`, [`a lined pond with air pumps`, `a steel tank with no outlet`, `a tank at 100 °C`], `Dung slurry is digested anaerobically. The gas collects under the floating cover and leaves through the pipe. Spent slurry is removed from another outlet.`);
mc(3, 'biogas', `Which of the following is NOT needed for biogas formation?`, `Plenty of oxygen`, [`Cattle dung`, `Anaerobic conditions`, `Methanogens`], `Methanogens are anaerobic bacteria. Oxygen would stop the process.`);
mc(3, 'biocontrol', `Bt toxin kills a larva when`, `the larva eats the spores and the toxin is released in its gut`, [`the spores are sprayed on the larva's skin`, `the plant makes antibiotics`, `the larva drinks water`], `The toxin is activated in the gut of the insect, damages it, and the larva dies. The spores are harmless to other insects.`);
mc(3, 'biocontrol', `Which of the following is NOT an advantage of biocontrol?`, `It acts quickly on all organisms in the field`, [`It has no harmful chemical residue`, `It is species-specific`, `It protects beneficial organisms`], `Biocontrol is specific and slower, which is why it is a part of integrated pest management.`);
mc(3, 'biocontrol', `Which of the following controls mosquitoes biologically?`, `Dragonflies`, [`Ladybirds`, `Trichoderma`, `Rhizobium`], `Dragonflies feed on mosquitoes. Ladybirds feed on aphids.`);
mc(3, 'biofertiliser', `Which of the following is a symbiotic N<sub>2</sub>-fixing microbe?`, `<i>Rhizobium</i>`, [`<i>Azotobacter</i>`, `<i>Azospirillum</i>`, `<i>Nostoc</i>`], `<i>Rhizobium</i> lives in the root nodules of legumes. The other three live freely in soil or water.`);
mc(3, 'biofertiliser', `Which of the following is a free-living nitrogen-fixing cyanobacterium?`, `<i>Nostoc</i>`, [`<i>Azotobacter</i>`, `<i>Rhizobium</i>`, `<i>Glomus</i>`], `<i>Nostoc</i> is a cyanobacterium. <i>Azotobacter</i> is a free-living bacterium that is not a cyanobacterium.`);
mc(3, 'biofertiliser', `Which of the following helps a plant to take up phosphorus?`, `<i>Glomus</i>`, [`<i>Rhizobium</i>`, `<i>Azospirillum</i>`, `<i>Anabaena</i>`], `<i>Glomus</i> forms mycorrhiza; its hyphae absorb phosphorus and pass it to the plant.`);
mc(3, 'biofertiliser', `A farmer grows pulses and wants to enrich the soil with nitrogen. He should inoculate the seeds with`, `<i>Rhizobium</i>`, [`<i>Trichoderma</i>`, `<i>Bacillus thuringiensis</i>`, `<i>Methanobacterium</i>`], `The pulse crop forms nodules with <i>Rhizobium</i>, which fixes nitrogen. <i>Trichoderma</i> and Bt are biocontrol agents.`);
mc(3, 'biofertiliser', `In which case does the microbe not fix nitrogen?`, `<i>Glomus</i>`, [`<i>Azotobacter</i>`, `<i>Anabaena</i>`, `<i>Rhizobium</i>`], `<i>Glomus</i> is a fungus that helps with phosphorus. The other three fix nitrogen.`);
mc(3, 'household', `Microbes include`, `bacteria, fungi, protozoa, viruses, viroids and prions`, [`bacteria only`, `bacteria and fungi only`, `bacteria and algae only`], `Microbes include all of these. In this chapter, we study bacteria, fungi and some viruses that are useful to us.`);

asr(3, 'household', `Curd is more nutritious than milk.`, `LAB increase the vitamin B<sub>12</sub> content of milk when they convert it to curd.`, 0, `The rise in B<sub>12</sub> is the NCERT reason curd is more nutritious. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'household', `Bread dough rises after the addition of baker's yeast.`, `Yeast produces CO<sub>2</sub> by fermentation of the sugars in the dough.`, 0, `The gas bubbles make the dough puff up. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'household', `Swiss cheese has large holes.`, `<i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i> produces a large amount of CO<sub>2</sub>.`, 0, `The gas collects as holes in the ripening cheese. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'industrial', `Penicillin was the first antibiotic to be discovered.`, `Fleming found that <i>Penicillium notatum</i> killed <i>Staphylococcus</i> bacteria.`, 0, `The observation led to the discovery of the first antibiotic. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'industrial', `Cyclosporin A is used to treat bacterial infections.`, `It is produced by the fungus <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>.`, 3, `Cyclosporin A is an immunosuppressant for organ transplant patients, not an antibiotic. A is false. R is true.`, `A fungus-produced drug is easily mistaken for an antibiotic.`);
asr(3, 'industrial', `Statins lower blood cholesterol.`, `Statins are competitive inhibitors of the enzyme responsible for the synthesis of cholesterol.`, 0, `The inhibition of the enzyme reduces cholesterol synthesis. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'sewage', `A sample with high BOD is more polluted than one with low BOD.`, `BOD is the amount of oxygen needed by bacteria to oxidise the organic matter in one litre of water.`, 0, `More organic matter needs more oxygen, which is why a higher BOD means higher pollution.`);
asr(3, 'sewage', `Primary treatment of sewage is a biological process.`, `In primary treatment, the floating debris and grit are removed.`, 3, `Primary treatment is physical (filtration and sedimentation). A is false. R is true.`);
asr(3, 'biogas', `Methanogens can be used for biogas production from cattle dung.`, `Methanogens are anaerobic bacteria that grow in the absence of oxygen.`, 0, `The digestion in a biogas plant is anaerobic, as methanogens need. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'biocontrol', `Bt is used in integrated pest management.`, `Bt spores kill all insects, both harmful and beneficial.`, 2, `Bt is used for biocontrol, so A is true. The toxin affects the specific larvae that eat the spores and the spores are harmless to other insects, so R is false.`);
asr(3, 'biofertiliser', `Cyanobacteria are useful in paddy fields.`, `Cyanobacteria fix atmospheric nitrogen and add organic matter to the soil.`, 0, `This enriches the soil. R explains A.`);
asr(3, 'biofertiliser', `Plants with mycorrhiza grow better in phosphorus-poor soil.`, `The fungal partner absorbs phosphorus from the soil and passes it to the plant.`, 0, `This is the main benefit named by NCERT. R explains A.`);

stm(3, 'household', `LAB are present in curd.`, `Yeast is used for setting curd.`, 2, `Curd is set by LAB. Yeast is used in bread and in making alcohol.`);
stm(3, 'industrial', `Penicillium notatum produces penicillin.`, `Trichoderma polysporum produces statins.`, 2, `<i>Trichoderma polysporum</i> produces cyclosporin A. Statins are from <i>Monascus purpureus</i>.`);
stm(3, 'industrial', `Whisky and rum are produced by fermentation and distillation.`, `Wine and beer are produced by fermentation without distillation.`, 0, `Both statements match NCERT.`);
stm(3, 'sewage', `Aerobic microbes grow as flocs in the aeration tank.`, `Anaerobic sludge digesters release oxygen.`, 2, `Anaerobic digesters release biogas (methane, H<sub>2</sub>S and CO<sub>2</sub>), not oxygen.`);
stm(3, 'biogas', `Biogas is rich in methane.`, `Biogas is used as a fuel for cooking and lighting.`, 0, `Both statements are true.`);
stm(3, 'biocontrol', `Baculoviruses are species-specific and have a narrow spectrum of action.`, `Baculoviruses are harmful to mammals and birds.`, 2, `They have no negative impact on plants, mammals, birds, fish or non-target insects.`);
stm(3, 'biofertiliser', `<i>Rhizobium</i> forms root nodules in cereals.`, `<i>Glomus</i> forms mycorrhiza.`, 3, `<i>Rhizobium</i> nodulates legumes, not cereals. Statement I is incorrect; II is correct.`);
stm(3, 'biofertiliser', `<i>Azotobacter</i> is symbiotic with legumes.`, `<i>Anabaena</i> is a fungus.`, 1, `<i>Azotobacter</i> is free-living, and <i>Anabaena</i> is a cyanobacterium. Both are incorrect.`);
stm(3, 'industrial', `Lipases are used in detergents.`, `Pectinases and proteases are used to clarify juices.`, 0, `Both statements are in NCERT.`);
stm(3, 'sewage', `BOD refers to the amount of oxygen consumed if all organic matter in one litre of water is oxidised by bacteria.`, `The lower the BOD, the greater the polluting potential.`, 2, `The higher the BOD, the more polluting the water. Statement II is incorrect.`);

match(3, 'industrial', 'mw-m1', 'Microbes and organic acids or ethanol', [`A. <i>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</i>`, `B. <i>Aspergillus niger</i>`, `C. <i>Acetobacter aceti</i>`, `D. <i>Clostridium butylicum</i>`], [`p. Butyric acid`, `q. Citric acid`, `r. Acetic acid`, `s. Ethanol`], `A-s, B-q, C-r, D-p`, [`A-q, B-s, C-r, D-p`, `A-s, B-q, C-p, D-r`, `A-r, B-q, C-s, D-p`], `Yeast gives ethanol (s). <i>A. niger</i> gives citric acid (q). <i>Acetobacter</i> gives acetic acid (r). <i>Clostridium</i> gives butyric acid (p).`);
match(3, 'industrial', 'mw-m2', 'Bioactive molecules and their sources', [`A. Cyclosporin A`, `B. Statins`, `C. Streptokinase`, `D. Penicillin`], [`p. <i>Monascus purpureus</i>`, `q. <i>Streptococcus</i>`, `r. <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i>`, `s. <i>Penicillium notatum</i>`], `A-r, B-p, C-q, D-s`, [`A-p, B-r, C-q, D-s`, `A-r, B-p, C-s, D-q`, `A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s`], `Cyclosporin A: <i>Trichoderma</i> (r). Statins: <i>Monascus</i> (p). Streptokinase: <i>Streptococcus</i> (q). Penicillin: <i>Penicillium</i> (s).`);
match(3, 'biofertiliser', 'mw-m3', 'Biofertilisers and their nature', [`A. <i>Rhizobium</i>`, `B. <i>Azotobacter</i>`, `C. <i>Anabaena</i>`, `D. <i>Glomus</i>`], [`p. Symbiotic N-fixing bacterium in legume nodules`, `q. Free-living N-fixing bacterium`, `r. Cyanobacterium`, `s. Mycorrhizal fungus`], `A-p, B-q, C-r, D-s`, [`A-q, B-p, C-r, D-s`, `A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r`, `A-r, B-q, C-p, D-s`], `Rhizobium: symbiotic (p). Azotobacter: free-living (q). Anabaena: cyanobacterium (r). Glomus: mycorrhiza (s).`);
match(3, 'biocontrol', 'mw-m4', 'Biocontrol agents and their actions', [`A. Bt`, `B. <i>Trichoderma</i>`, `C. Baculovirus`, `D. Ladybird`], [`p. Insect virus that is species-specific`, `q. Free-living fungus that acts against plant pathogens`, `r. Beetle that eats aphids`, `s. Bacterial spores that make a toxin in the gut of larvae`], `A-s, B-q, C-p, D-r`, [`A-q, B-s, C-p, D-r`, `A-s, B-q, C-r, D-p`, `A-p, B-q, C-s, D-r`], `Bt: toxin from spores in larval gut (s). <i>Trichoderma</i>: fungus against pathogens (q). Baculovirus: insect virus (p). Ladybird: eats aphids (r).`);
match(3, 'household', 'mw-m5', 'Household products and the microbes responsible', [`A. Curd`, `B. Dough of bread`, `C. Swiss cheese`, `D. Roquefort cheese`], [`p. <i>Propionibacterium sharmanii</i>`, `q. Specific fungi`, `r. Lactic acid bacteria`, `s. Baker's yeast`], `A-r, B-s, C-p, D-q`, [`A-s, B-r, C-p, D-q`, `A-r, B-s, C-q, D-p`, `A-p, B-s, C-r, D-q`], `Curd: LAB (r). Bread: yeast (s). Swiss cheese: <i>Propionibacterium</i> (p). Roquefort: fungi (q).`);

pass('mw-p1', `A sewage treatment plant`, `In a town's sewage treatment plant, raw sewage first passes through screens and a sedimentation tank. The effluent then goes to a large tank where air is pumped in and the liquid is constantly stirred. After some hours, the liquid is allowed to settle. A part of the settled material is returned to the first tank, and the rest is sent to a closed tank without air.`);
pq('mw-p1', 3, 'sewage', `The settled material that is partly returned to the aeration tank is`, `activated sludge`, [`primary sludge`, `grit`, `biogas`], `The flocs that settle after aeration form the activated sludge. Part of it is used as inoculum.`);
pq('mw-p1', 3, 'sewage', `The microbes in the last closed tank are`, `anaerobic bacteria`, [`aerobic bacteria`, `photosynthetic bacteria`, `viruses`], `Because there is no air, anaerobic bacteria digest the sludge and release biogas.`);
pq('mw-p1', 4, 'sewage', `Which step lowers BOD the most?`, `the aeration tank`, [`the screens`, `the sedimentation tank`, `the closed tank`], `Aerobic flocs consume most of the organic matter in the effluent. The screens and sedimentation tank only remove solids; digestion treats the sludge, not the effluent.`);

pass('mw-p2', `A village farmer`, `A farmer has a paddy field, a pulse field and an orchard on poor soil. He wants to cut down on chemical fertilisers and pesticides. The soils are low in nitrogen. The roots of the orchard trees show little fungal association and the soil is low in phosphorus. Cabbage plants in his kitchen garden are attacked by caterpillars.`);
pq('mw-p2', 3, 'biofertiliser', `Which biofertiliser is best for the paddy field?`, `Cyanobacteria such as <i>Anabaena</i>`, [`<i>Glomus</i>`, `<i>Trichoderma</i>`, `<i>Rhizobium</i>`], `Cyanobacteria fix nitrogen in flooded paddy fields. <i>Rhizobium</i> needs legumes.`);
pq('mw-p2', 3, 'biofertiliser', `For the orchard soil low in phosphorus, the most suitable choice is`, `<i>Glomus</i>`, [`<i>Azotobacter</i>`, `<i>Bt</i>`, `<i>Methanobacterium</i>`], `<i>Glomus</i> forms mycorrhiza that helps in phosphorus uptake.`);
pq('mw-p2', 3, 'biocontrol', `For the caterpillars on cabbage, the best biological option is`, `spraying dried Bt spores in water`, [`spraying <i>Rhizobium</i>`, `spraying cyanobacteria`, `adding mycorrhiza`], `Bt kills larvae of such pests and is a standard biocontrol for vegetables like brassicas.`);

pass('mw-p3', `A gobar gas plant`, `A village family uses a gobar gas plant. Each day they mix cattle dung with water and feed it into a large tank. A floating drum above the slurry rises slowly through the day. A pipe takes gas from the drum to the kitchen. The thick slurry that comes out of a second pipe is spread on the field.`);
pq('mw-p3', 3, 'biogas', `The gas that burns in the kitchen is mainly`, `methane`, [`oxygen`, `chlorine`, `hydrogen chloride`], `Methane is the main fuel gas in biogas.`);
pq('mw-p3', 3, 'biogas', `The microbes that make the gas belong to the group`, `methanogens`, [`nitrifiers`, `lactic acid bacteria`, `mycorrhizal fungi`], `Methanogens (such as <i>Methanobacterium</i>) act on the dung in the absence of oxygen.`);
pq('mw-p3', 3, 'biogas', `Why does the drum rise during the day?`, `Gas collects below it as the dung is digested`, [`Air is blown in`, `The dung freezes`, `The slurry grows microbes with oxygen`], `The volume of the gas increases and pushes the floating cover up.`);

nat(3, 'sewage', `A sewage sample has a BOD of 300 mg/L. After secondary treatment the BOD is 30 mg/L. By what percentage has the BOD decreased?`, 90, `Decrease = (300 - 30) / 300 = 0.9, which is 90%.`, '%');
nat(3, 'sewage', `A sample has a BOD of 240 mg of oxygen per litre. How many mg of oxygen will be consumed by microbes in 5 L of this sample?`, 1200, `Oxygen demand = 240 mg/L × 5 L = 1200 mg.`, 'mg');
nat(3, 'industrial', `In 1928 Fleming noticed the effect of a mould on bacteria. In 1945 he, Chain and Florey got the Nobel Prize. How many years later was the prize?`, 17, `1945 - 1928 = 17 years.`, 'years');
nat(3, 'industrial', `Among whisky, wine, brandy, beer and rum, how many need distillation after fermentation?`, 3, `Whisky, brandy and rum are distilled. Wine and beer are not. So 3.`);
nat(3, 'industrial', `Among <i>Aspergillus niger</i>, <i>Acetobacter aceti</i>, <i>Clostridium butylicum</i>, <i>Lactobacillus</i>, <i>Penicillium notatum</i>, <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i> and <i>Monascus purpureus</i>, how many are fungi?`, 4, `Fungi: <i>Aspergillus niger</i>, <i>Penicillium notatum</i>, <i>Trichoderma polysporum</i> and <i>Monascus purpureus</i> (a yeast). The other three are bacteria. So 4.`);
nat(3, 'biofertiliser', `Among <i>Rhizobium</i>, <i>Azotobacter</i>, <i>Azospirillum</i>, <i>Anabaena</i>, <i>Nostoc</i>, <i>Oscillatoria</i> and <i>Glomus</i>, how many are cyanobacteria?`, 3, `<i>Anabaena</i>, <i>Nostoc</i> and <i>Oscillatoria</i> are cyanobacteria. So 3.`);

